# Library Management System

## Problem Statement

Libraries manage many books and need a simple way to keep track of their records. Managing book information manually can make it difficult to add new books, search for a particular book, view available records, and remove outdated records.

The Library Management System provides a simple Python-based solution for managing basic book records. It allows the user to add, view, search, and delete books through a menu-driven interface.

## Scope

The project focuses on basic library book management. Each book record contains a book ID, title, author, category, and publication year. The records are stored in a JSON file so that the information can be accessed when the program is used again.

## Target Users

* Students learning Python programming
* Teachers demonstrating basic file handling and data management
* Small library-management demonstrations
* Beginners developing their first Python project

## Main Features

1. Add a new book
2. View all books
3. Search for a book using its ID
4. Delete a book record
5. Store book records in JSON format
6. Validate basic user input
7. Display library information in a simple format
8. Run automated tests for important operations

## Technologies Used

The project is developed using Python 3 and uses the standard Python library. JSON is used for storing book records. No external Python packages are required.

## Expected Outcome

The expected outcome is a working command-line Library Management System that demonstrates basic Python programming concepts while providing useful operations for managing book records.
